WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.630
From 2018, the US federal
tax rate on corporate

2
00:00:03.630 --> 00:00:07.950
profits fell from 35
percent to 21 percent.

3
00:00:07.950 --> 00:00:10.280
Supporters said firms would invest more,

4
00:00:10.280 --> 00:00:12.270
and workers would earn more.

5
00:00:12.270 --> 00:00:16.180
One 2024 study estimated
that investment did rise,

6
00:00:16.180 --> 00:00:17.900
by about 11 percent.

7
00:00:17.900 --> 00:00:22.000
But wages and growth rose by
less than supporters had claimed.

8
00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:25.900
So how can a government raise
the most its economy can produce,

9
00:00:25.900 --> 00:00:28.010
and why does it take so long?

10
00:00:28.010 --> 00:00:30.680
In this mission, you'll
see how policy can move

11
00:00:30.680 --> 00:00:33.250
the long-run aggregate supply curve.

12
00:00:33.250 --> 00:00:36.520
Then you'll build roads and
broadband in a graph lab,

13
00:00:36.520 --> 00:00:39.330
and compare the short
run with the long run.

14
00:00:39.330 --> 00:00:43.410
Your mission: find out which
policies raise potential output,

15
00:00:43.410 --> 00:00:45.090
and why they take years.
